1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:09,077
Question five. Highlight: an online article claims “all social posts are untrustworthy”; ask what information literacy looks like.

2
00:00:09,077 --> 00:00:14,454
Useful: literacy = verify, then judge — neither blind trust nor blind reject.

3
00:00:14,454 --> 00:00:19,761
Useless: how sensational the headline is — does not decide the right action.

4
00:00:19,761 --> 00:00:23,810
Option A. Forward at once — spreading without check — cut.

5
00:00:23,810 --> 00:00:28,489
Option B. Delete because the title is loud, and never verify — cut.

6
00:00:28,489 --> 00:00:33,865
Option C. Check author, date, citations and other reports, then judge — keep.

7
00:00:33,865 --> 00:00:37,077
Option D. Conclude from the title alone — cut.

8
00:00:37,077 --> 00:00:40,778
Literacy centres on verifying sources before judging.

9
00:00:40,778 --> 00:00:43,152
Therefore the correct answer is C.

